# Line endings are a product concern here, not just a developer preference.
#
# phantom SHIPS text files inside its npm tarball and reads them verbatim at
# runtime: templates/post-mortem.md is embedded in the prompt, the plugin's
# SKILL.md has its YAML frontmatter stripped with an LF-anchored regex, and
# bin/*.js carry a `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang that POSIX kernels reject the
# moment a CR sneaks in ("env: node\r: No such file or directory"). Windows
# checkouts default to core.autocrlf=true, so without this file a package
# published from Windows would ship CRLF templates and broken bins.
#
# Normalize everything to LF in the working tree on every platform. There are
# no .bat/.cmd/.ps1 files in this repo, so nothing here needs CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never inspected for line endings, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.mp4 binary
